[Event "Strategy: the pawn break, lesson"]
[Result "1-0"]
[Variant "Standard"]
[ChapterURL "https://lichess.org/study/Hc5NIk9A/BOe48Lw4"]
[FEN "r2q1rk1/pp2b2p/2n1bpp1/3p1p2/1PP5/P3PN2/3NBPPP/R2Q1RK1 w - - 1 14"]
[SetUp "1"]
[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/r2q1rk1/pp2b2p/2n1bpp1/3p1p2/1PP5/P3PN2/3NBPPP/R2Q1RK1_w_-_-_1_14"]

{ Pawns never move backwards. Today: when to push them, and when to let them go. First plan: the pawn break. [%cal Yc4c5] }
14. c5 { Pawn to c5! Release the tension now: his bishop on e7 is shut in, and b5 and c6 will roll. [%csl Gc5][%cal Gb4b5,Gc5c6] } (14. Qb3 { The queen presses on d5, and he simply takes. } 14... dxc4 15. Bxc4 Bxc4 16. Qxc4+ { The tension is gone and so is your bind. Only a little better. }) (14. Qa4 { A queen move, and he pins your pawns with a5. } 14... a5 15. b5 Ne5 { Playable, but his knight lands on e5. Only a little better. }) (14. Qc2 { Quiet, and he plays a5 himself. } 14... a5 15. b5 Ne5 { Only a little better. }) (14. Rc1 { The rook is ready, and he trades on c4. } 14... dxc4 15. Qa4 a6 16. Bxc4 { The centre is open. Only a little better. }) (14. cxd5 { You release the tension the wrong way. } 14... Bxd5 15. Qa4 a6 { His bishop sits on d5, a monster. Only a little better. [%csl Rd5] }) 14... a6 { He stops b5 for now. Bring the knight to d4. [%cal Yf3d4] } 15. Nd4 { Knight to d4: it hits his knight, and after the trade the d4 pawn will support c5 and b5. [%csl Gd4] } (15. Nb3 { Also good. The knight guards c5 and a5. } 15... Bf7 16. Nfd4 Ne5 { Still winning. }) (15. Re1 { Fine, but the knight was ready. } 15... Qd7 16. Nd4 Nxd4 17. exd4 { The same, a move later. }) (15. Qc2 { Also fine. } 15... Re8 16. Nd4 Nxd4 17. exd4 { The same. }) (15. Rb1 { Slow, and he tidies. } 15... Qd7 16. Re1 Rfe8 { Still better. }) 15... Nxd4 { He trades. Take back with the pawn. [%cal Ye3d4] } 16. exd4 { The pawn takes back: now c5 has a friend on d4, and b5 followed by c6 is coming. [%csl Gd4,Gc5][%cal Gb4b5,Gc5c6] } 1-0


[Event "Strategy: the pawn break, right away"]
[Result "1-0"]
[Variant "Standard"]
[ChapterURL "https://lichess.org/study/Hc5NIk9A/Bzn7Sw7H"]
[FEN "r4rk1/2R3bp/5ppn/p2pp3/4b3/1P2P3/PB1NBPPP/3R2K1 b - - 3 19"]
[SetUp "1"]
[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/r4rk1/2R3bp/5ppn/p2pp3/4b3/1P2P3/PB1NBPPP/3R2K1_b_-_-_3_19"]

{ You want the pawn break e4. He keeps hitting your pieces to delay it. When do you push? }
19... Bf5 { The bishop is back, and it stares at e4. Do you chase it first, or push now? } 20. e4 { Right away! Who cares about a pawn: the hit on the bishop matters, and he gets no protected passer. [%csl Ge4][%cal Ge4f5] } (20. Bb5 { A good square, but slow. } 20... Rfc8 21. Rdc1 Rxc7 22. Rxc7 { Still better, but the break is not in. }) (20. a4 { A pawn move on the side. } 20... Rfd8 21. h3 Be6 { He tidies up. Only a little better. }) (20. Bf3 { The bishop hits d5, and he pushes past. } 20... Be6 21. Nb1 e4 { His pawns roll. Only a little better. [%csl Re4] }) (20. h3 { You chase the bishop first, and he gets d4 in. } 20... Rfd8 21. g4 Be6 22. e4 d4 { A protected passed pawn for him. Equal. [%csl Rd4] }) 20... dxe4 { He takes. Now the check. } 21. Bc4+ { Check, and the bishop lands on the diagonal he just opened. [%cal Gc4g8] } (21. h3 { Slow. } 21... Rfd8 22. Bc3 a4 { Still better, but he untangles. }) (21. Nc4 { The knight goes hunting and ends in the corner. } 21... Rf7 22. Nb6 Rxc7 23. Nxa8 { You win the exchange, and the knight is stuck on a8. Still better. [%csl Ra8] }) (21. Nxe4 { You take the pawn back, and the bishop pair is his. } 21... Bxe4 22. Rdd7 Nf5 { Equal. [%csl Re4] }) (21. Bc3 { The bishop hits a5. } 21... a4 22. bxa4 Rfc8 { Only a little better. }) 21... Kh8 { The king hides. Now the knight. } 22. Nf1 { Knight to f1, then e3: the e4 pawn is a target and f5 is under fire. [%cal Gf1e3,Ge3f5][%csl Re4] } (22. h3 { Slow, and he tidies up. } 22... Rfd8 23. Bc3 Bf8 { Only a little better. }) (22. Bc3 { The bishop hits a5, and he trades rooks. } 22... Rfd8 23. Re1 Rd7 { Only a little better. }) (22. Re1 { The rook hits e4, and he trades. } 22... Rfc8 23. Rxc8+ Rxc8 { Only a little better. }) (22. a4 { A pawn move. } 22... Rfd8 23. Bc3 Ng4 { Only a little better. }) 1-0


