{ His pawns are doubled on the f column. A better structure wins nothing by itself: you need a file. Which pawn? [%csl Rf6,Rf7] }
17. f3 { Pawn to f3: the f column opens, straight onto the doubled pawns. [%cal Gf3e4,Gf1f7][%csl Rf7] } (17. f4 { You close the position, and the doubled pawns are safe behind the wall. } 17... f5 18. Rc3 Rhc8 { Only a little better. [%csl Rf4] }) (17. Rfd1 { A rook move. Fine, but the file was the point. } 17... Rac8 18. d3 f5 { Still better. }) (17. Rc3 { The rook lifts, and he trades. } 17... a5 18. Rfc1 Rhb8 { Only a little better. }) (17. g3 { Slow. } 17... f5 18. Rfd1 Rac8 { Only a little better. }) 1-0


