{ You have a break in the centre. Do you prepare it, or play it now? }
10. d5 { Play it now! The pawn cramps him, and e4 comes next. Prepare it, and he stops it. [%csl Gd5][%cal Ge3e4] } (10. Qc2 { Preparing a move you could play at once. } 10... cxd4 11. Nxd4 Rc8 { He traded first. Equal. }) (10. Rc1 { A rook move, and he trades. } 10... a6 11. Bd3 cxd4 { Only a little better. }) (10. Re1 { Slow. } 10... a6 11. Qc2 cxd4 { Only a little better. }) (10. dxc5 { You release the tension for nothing. } 10... Nxc5 11. Qc2 Rc8 { His knight lands on c5. Equal. [%csl Gc5] }) (10. h3 { A pawn move on the edge. } 10... a6 11. Rc1 Re8 { Only a little better. }) 1-0


