[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/r1bq1rk1/4bppp/p1n1pn2/1p6/3P4/P1N2N2/BP3PPP/R1BQR1K1_w_-_-_0_13"]

{ New plan: the isolated pawn. Weak in the endgame, strong in the middlegame. His knight left d5. Push! [%cal Yd4d5] }
13. d5 { The break! His knight left d5, and now the pawn opens every line while his pieces are still at home. [%csl Gd5] } (13. Qd3 { You prepare, and he plays b4. } 13... Bb7 14. Bg5 b4 { The break is gone. Only a little better. }) (13. Bg5 { Development, and the moment passes. } 13... h6 14. Bh4 b4 { Only a little better. }) (13. h3 { Slow. } 13... Bb7 14. d5 Nxd5 { He is ready for it now. Only a little better. }) (13. Ne5 { The knight jumps, and the pawn falls. } 13... Nxd4 14. Be3 Nf5 { A pawn gone. Worse. [%csl Rd4] }) 13... exd5 { He takes. Take back with the knight. [%cal Yc3d5] } 14. Nxd5 { The knight sits in the middle, and every black piece is hit or pinned. [%csl Gd5][%cal Gd5e7,Gd5f6] } (14. Bxd5 { The bishop takes, and everything gets traded. } 14... Nxd5 15. Nxd5 Be6 { The pressure is gone. Equal. }) (14. Qd3 { Slow. } 14... Be6 15. Ng5 Qd7 { He has caught up. Slightly worse. }) (14. Bg5 { The pin, but he untangles. } 14... Be6 15. Rc1 Rc8 { Slightly worse. }) 14... Ra7 { The rook guards e7. Now develop with a hit. [%cal Yc1e3] } 15. Be3 { Bishop to e3, aiming at a7 and b6. Every piece joins in. [%cal Ge3a7][%csl Gd5] } (15. Bf4 { Also fine. } 15... Rd7 16. Nxe7+ Nxe7 { Still better. }) (15. Nxe7+ { You trade the monster. } 15... Rxe7 16. Bd2 Bg4 { Slightly better only. }) (15. Qc2 { The queen comes out, and he takes on d5. } 15... Nxd5 16. Qxc6 Bb7 { Equal. }) (15. h3 { Slow. } 15... Be6 16. Nxe7+ Rxe7 { Only a little better. }) 1-0


[Event "Strategy: the isolani, keep the lid on"]
[Result "0-1"]
[Variant "Standard"]
[ChapterURL "https://lichess.org/study/Hc5NIk9A/Tn2qTkzD"]
[FEN "r1bq1rk1/pp2bppp/2n1p3/3n4/2BP4/2N2N2/PP3PPP/R1BQ1RK1 w - - 1 10"]
[SetUp "1"]
[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/r1bq1rk1/pp2bppp/2n1p3/3n4/2BP4/2N2N2/PP3PPP/R1BQ1RK1_w_-_-_1_10"]

{ His pawn on d4 is isolated, and your knight on d5 blocks it cold. Prying it loose is his whole plan. Keep the lid on. }
10. Re1 { His rook lines up on the e column. Which piece must not leave d5? [%csl Gd5] } 10... Bf6 { Bishop to f6: it piles onto d4, and the knight is not going anywhere. His pawn can never push to d5 now. [%cal Gf6d4][%csl Gd5] } (10... Nf6 { The knight leaves the blockade, and the break is on. } 11. a3 b6 12. Ba2 Bb7 13. Bf4 { The knight is gone, so d4-d5 is coming next. Slightly worse. [%cal Rd4d5] }) (10... a6 { Slow. b5 will only make d5 stronger. } 11. Bb3 Nf6 12. a3 b5 13. d5 { There it is. Slightly worse. [%csl Rd5] }) (10... Bd6 { A fine square, but Ne5 hits it. } 11. Bb3 h6 12. Bd2 Nce7 13. Ne5 { Slightly worse. }) (10... Nxc3 { You trade the blockader. } 11. bxc3 b6 12. h4 Bb7 13. Ng5 { His pieces come at your king. Slightly worse. }) (10... h6 { A pawn move, and he improves. } 11. Qe2 Bd6 12. Bd2 b6 { Slightly worse. }) 0-1


[Event "Strategy: the isolani, chase the bishop"]
[Result "0-1"]
[Variant "Standard"]
[ChapterURL "https://lichess.org/study/Hc5NIk9A/FMxJOcuY"]
[FEN "r2q1rk1/1p1bbppp/p1n1pn2/6B1/3P4/1BN2N2/PP1Q1PPP/R4RK1 w - - 5 12"]
[SetUp "1"]
[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/r2q1rk1/1p1bbppp/p1n1pn2/6B1/3P4/1BN2N2/PP1Q1PPP/R4RK1_w_-_-_5_12"]

{ He has the isolani on d4, and everything is in place to push it to d5. His bishop on b3 is what makes that push work. [%csl Rb3][%cal Rd4d5] }
12. Rad1 { The rook joins in. d5 is in the air. Which piece must go? [%cal Rd4d5] } 12... Na5 { Knight to a5: it chases the bishop off the diagonal, and the d5 break loses its bite. [%cal Ga5b3][%csl Rb3] } (12... Rc8 { Natural, and the break lands. } 13. d5 exd5 14. Nxd5 Be6 15. Nxe7+ { The centre opened while you were not ready. Slightly worse. [%csl Rd5] }) (12... Nb4 { The other way round the bishop. } 13. Ne5 Bc6 14. f4 { His pieces roll forward. Worse. }) (12... h6 { You kick the bishop, and it takes. } 13. Bxh6 Nd5 14. Rfe1 { A pawn gone and your king is open. Worse. [%csl Rh6] }) (12... Re8 { Slow. } 13. Rfe1 h6 14. Bxh6 { The same trick. Worse. }) (12... Qa5 { The queen comes out, and nothing changes. } 13. Rfe1 Rad8 14. h3 { Worse. }) 13. Bc2 { The bishop steps to c2. Keep going. } 13... Nc4 { Knight to c4: it hits the queen and b2, and the bishop on c2 has no diagonal. [%csl Gc4][%cal Gc4d2] } (13... Rc8 { Also fine, but the knight was ready to jump. } 14. Bd3 Nc4 15. Bxc4 Rxc4 { Equal. }) (13... Bc6 { The bishop moves, and his knight jumps. } 14. Ne5 b5 15. Qd3 { Slightly worse. [%csl Re5] }) (13... g6 { A hole for nothing. } 14. Ne5 Bb5 15. Rfe1 { Worse. }) (13... Bb5 { The bishop comes out, and the h column opens. } 14. Rfe1 Nc4 15. Qf4 { Worse. }) 0-1


[Event "Strategy: the isolani, take it on purpose"]
[Result "0-1"]
[Variant "Standard"]
[ChapterURL "https://lichess.org/study/Hc5NIk9A/KG53RfuA"]
[FEN "r2qkb1r/3npppp/p1p2n2/3p4/NpPP4/1P2PQ1P/P2B1PP1/R3KB1R b KQkq - 1 10"]
