{ You have the good bishop and his knight is far from d4. Is an isolated pawn a price worth paying? [%csl Ra4] }
10... e5 { Yes! Pawn to e5. You take an isolani, and in return your bishop gets the b8 to h2 diagonal. [%cal Ge5d4][%csl Ra4] } (10... Ne4 { The knight jumps, and he trades it. } 11. Bd3 Nxd2 12. Kxd2 e6 { Solid and a bit passive. Slightly worse. }) (10... Qb8 { The queen hides. } 11. g4 e5 12. g5 { His pawns come. Slightly worse. }) (10... e6 { Solid, and your bishop stays behind the pawns. } 11. Bd3 Be7 12. e4 { He has the centre and you have nothing. Slightly worse. [%csl Rc8] }) (10... h5 { A pawn move on the edge. } 11. cxd5 cxd5 12. Rc1 { Worse. }) (10... dxc4 { You take, and his bishop comes out with a hit. } 11. Bxc4 a5 12. Rc1 { c6 hangs and his pieces are ready. Worse. [%csl Rc6] }) 11. Qe2 { His queen steps back. Bring out the bishop. } 11... Bd6 { Bishop to d6: it eyes h2, and the pawn on e5 is guarded. [%cal Gd6h2] } (11... h5 { A pawn move first. Also fine. } 12. g3 Bd6 { The bishop comes anyway. }) (11... Be7 { The wrong diagonal, and he closes the centre. } 12. g3 e4 { Your bishop is passive. Slightly worse. }) (11... Ne4 { The knight jumps first. } 12. g3 Bd6 13. Bg2 { Fine, but slower. }) (11... g6 { A hole for nothing. } 12. g4 Qe7 { Slightly worse. }) 12. g3 { He guards h2. Castle. } 12... O-O { Castle. Now the rooks come to the e column. [%csl Gg8] } (12... a5 { A pawn move first. Also fine. } 13. Rc1 O-O { Castle next. }) (12... h5 { You go for the king, but yours is still in the middle. } 13. Bg2 a5 { Slightly worse. }) (12... Ne4 { The knight jumps, and he takes on e5. } 13. Bg2 a5 14. dxe5 { Slightly worse. }) (12... Qe7 { The queen moves, and c5 hits. } 13. c5 Bc7 14. Bxb4 { A pawn gone. Worse. [%csl Rb4] }) 13. dxe5 { He takes. Take back with the bishop. } 13... Bxe5 { The bishop takes back and sits on e5, staring at b2 and h2. The isolani was worth it. [%csl Ge5][%cal Ge5b2,Ge5h2] } (13... Nxe5 { The knight takes, and the bishop stays home. } 14. cxd5 cxd5 15. Bg2 { Fine, but the bishop was the point. Slightly worse. }) (13... dxc4 { You leave a piece hanging. } 14. exd6 { A whole bishop. [%csl Rd6] }) (13... Ne4 { The knight jumps, and the bishop is lost. } 14. exd6 { A whole bishop. [%csl Rd6] }) 0-1


