{ His isolated pawn on d5 is a weakness, and he has no dark bishop to make trouble. Where do your rooks want to go? [%csl Rd5] }
29... Nd7 { The knight steps back. The c column is open. Take it. } 30. Rc3 { Rook to c3: you fight for the only open column, and the queen comes to c1 behind it. [%cal Gc3c8,Gb1c1] } (30. Qa1 { The queen goes to the corner. } 30... Nd6 31. Bg3 Qf6 { Slightly better, but the column is not yours. }) (30. Bg3 { You hit the queen, and she steps aside. } 30... Qg5 31. Bf2 Qg6 { Slightly better only. }) (30. h4 { A pawn move on the side. } 30... Nf8 31. Qa1 Ne6 { Slightly better. }) (30. h3 { Slow. } 30... Nf8 31. Rc3 Nd2 { Only a little better. }) 30... Nf8 { He regroups. Now the queen behind the rook. } 31. Qc1 { Queen to c1: the c column is a battery now, and his knight on c4 is pinned to the rook. [%cal Gc1c8][%csl Rc4] } (31. Qc2 { The queen goes to c2 and blocks its own rook. } 31... Qe8 32. Qc1 Ne6 { You go to c1 anyway. Slightly better. }) (31. Bg3 { You hit the queen, and she steps away. } 31... Qe8 32. Qc1 a5 { Slightly better. }) (31. Qf5 { The queen wanders. } 31... Qe8 32. Qb1 Nd2 { Only a little better. }) (31. h3 { Slow, and his knight jumps. } 31... Nd2 32. Qc2 Nxf1 { Only a little better. }) 31... Ne6 { He hits your knight. Now the pawn. } 32. b3 { Pawn to b3: the knight on c4 must go, and the c column is yours. [%cal Gb3c4][%csl Gc3] } (32. Bg3 { You hit the queen, and he trades on d4. } 32... Qf6 33. b3 Nxd4 { Only a little better. }) (32. Bd3 { The bishop hits the knight, and he trades knights. } 32... Nxd4 33. exd4 Qe8 { Only a little better. }) (32. Ne2 { The knight retreats. } 32... Rc6 33. h3 Qf6 { Only a little better. }) (32. h4 { A pawn move. } 32... Nxd4 33. exd4 Qe6 { Only a little better. }) 1-0


