{ His pawns are on a7, b6 and c7: the minority attack is over. There is another break. Which pawn? [%csl Gd5] }
21. e4 { Pawn to e4! The centre blows open, and every white piece points at his king. [%csl Ge4][%cal Gd3h7] } (21. Rbc1 { A rook move, and the position stays closed. } 21... Bg7 22. Ne2 Ne8 { Still better, but slow. }) (21. f4 { The other pawn, and his knight lands on e4. } 21... Qe7 22. Nf3 Ne4 { Still better, but e4 is his. [%csl Re4] }) (21. Rbd1 { Slow. } 21... Bg7 22. Qb3 Kh7 { Still better. }) (21. Nf3 { The knight goes to f3 and his knight jumps to e4. } 21... Ne4 22. Bxe4 dxe4 { Still better, but e4 is gone. [%csl Re4] }) 21... Nh5 { The knight jumps to the rim. Take on d5. } 22. Nxd5 { Knight takes d5! The bishop must take back, and then the pawn recaptures with a monster on d5. [%cal Gb7d5,Ge4d5] } (22. Be2 { You hit the knight first. Also good. } 22... Ng7 23. exd5 Qf6 { Still winning. }) (22. exd5 { The pawn takes. Also good, the same thing in another order. } 22... Qf6 23. Nf3 Nf4 { Still winning. }) (22. Nf3 { Slow. } 22... Nf4 23. exd5 Qd6 { Still better. }) (22. e5 { You close it again. } 22... Nf4 23. Nf1 c6 { His knight sits on f4. Still better, but less. [%csl Rf4] }) 22... Bxd5 { He takes back. Recapture. } 23. exd5 { A pawn sits on d5, his queen is hit, and the bishop on d3 stares at his king. [%csl Gd5][%cal Gd3h7] } 1-0


