{ Both sides have a backward pawn: yours on c3, his on b6. His wants to run to b5. Stop it, for ever. [%csl Rb6,Rc3] }
1. a4 { Pawn to a4: b5 is never coming. The b6 pawn is fixed, and your rook will come to b1 to eat it. [%csl Rb6][%cal Gf1b1] } (1. Rb1 { The rook first, and he runs. } 1... a4 2. Qxb6 g5 { A messy fight. Only a little better. [%csl Ra4] }) (1. Qxb6 { You grab the pawn, and his rook wakes up. } 1... Rb8 2. Qa6 Bh6 { A pawn up, but his pieces are alive. Only a little better. }) (1. Re1 { A rook move, and b5 comes. } 1... b5 2. e6 fxe6 { Equal. [%csl Gb5] }) (1. h3 { Slow, and b5 comes. } 1... b5 2. Qxb5 Nxe5 { Equal. }) 1-0


