{ New plan: give a pawn, get the game. He wants d6 and castles. One pawn push wrecks his structure for ever. [%cal Yd5d6] }
9. d6 { Pawn to d6! He must take, and his pawns are doubled on the d column for good. A pawn well spent. [%csl Gd6] } (9. Qh6 { Also strong: the queen stops him castling. But he keeps his structure. } 9... d6 10. Nf3 Nd7 { A normal game. Still better. }) (9. Nf3 { Also good. } 9... O-O 10. Qh6 Bb4+ { Fine, but no wrecked pawns. }) (9. Bd2 { Development, and he castles. } 9... O-O 10. Bc3 Bf6 { Only a little better. }) (9. h4 { A pawn on the edge. } 9... O-O 10. Nf3 Re8 { Only a little better. }) (9. Qxe7+ { The queens go, and your d pawn is lost. } 9... Qxe7 10. Nf3 Na6 { The d5 pawn falls next. Lost. [%csl Rd5] }) 9... cxd6 { He takes. Now the knight: to h3, then f4 and d5. [%cal Yg1h3,Gh3f4] } 10. Nh3 { Knight to h3, on its way to f4 and d5. His d pawns are doubled and weak for ever. [%cal Gh3f4,Gf4d5][%csl Rd6] } (10. Bg2 { The bishop first. Fine, but the knight has a road. } 10... Nc6 11. Bd2 O-O { Still better. }) (10. Bd2 { Slow. } 10... O-O 11. Bg2 Nc6 { Still better. }) (10. h4 { The pawn storm without the pieces. } 10... Nc6 11. Nf3 d5 { Only a little better. }) (10. Qd3 { The queen hits d6, and he develops. } 10... Nc6 11. Bg2 O-O { Only a little better. }) 1-0


