{ You are under pressure: his rook wants c7 and his queen wants h5. Castling loses a pawn. Is that a price worth paying? }
17. Rxc1 { He takes back. Your queen is overloaded. What now? [%csl Rc7] } 17... O-O { Castle! Yes, a pawn goes, but your king is safe and your pieces are free. [%csl Gg8] } (17... Bxf3 { You trade first, and his queen gets f3. } 18. Qxf3 Bxg5 19. hxg5 O-O { Also fine, but you helped his queen. }) (17... Bc6 { You guard the pawn, and the king stays in the middle. } 18. Bxe7 Kxe7 19. Qa6 { The a pawn falls and your king is stuck. Slightly worse. [%csl Re7] }) (17... h6 { You kick the bishop, and the king stays home. } 18. Bxe7 Kxe7 19. Nd2 { Slightly worse. }) (17... Qa8 { The queen goes to the corner to guard pawns. Passive. } 18. Nd2 Bd5 19. Nc4 { Your queen is stuck guarding pawns. Worse. [%csl Ra8] }) 18. Bxe7 { He takes the bishop. Take back. } 18... Qxe7 { The queen takes back. He will grab a7, and you get h6, rook d8 and an open board. [%csl Gg8][%cal Gf8d8] } 0-1


[Event "Strategy: give a pawn, keep what you have"]
