{ He wants to play f4 himself, and free his position. One pawn move denies him that — for the price of a pawn. }
16... f4 { Pawn to f4! The bishop takes it, but his pawns are stuck on light squares for good, and f4 is never his. [%csl Rf3,Re4][%cal Gf8f7] } (16... Rf7 { A useful move, and he gets f4 in first. } 17. f4 Ng4 18. Bd4 { His bishop is happy. Equal. [%csl Gf4] }) (16... Bd7 { Development, and f4 comes. } 17. f4 Ng4 18. Bd4 { Equal. }) (16... Nf7 { The knight retreats, and his knight jumps. } 17. Nb5 fxe4 18. fxe4 { Slightly worse. }) (16... Bf6 { The bishop moves, and he takes the diagonal. } 17. Bd4 f4 18. Nb5 { Slightly worse. }) (16... Nxf3+ { A pawn with check, and the knight is lost. } 17. Bxf3 { A knight for a pawn. [%csl Rf3] }) 17. Bxf4 { He takes. Now the f column. } 17... Rf7 { Rook to f7: the f column is yours, the bishop on f4 is a target, and the queen comes to f8. [%cal Gf7f4,Gd8f8] } (17... Bd7 { Also playable. The exchange sacrifice comes a move later. } 18. Nd1 Rxf4 19. Qxf4 Bh6 { Equal. }) (17... b6 { A pawn move, and he castles. } 18. axb6 Qxb6 19. O-O { Slightly worse. }) (17... Rf6 { The rook on f6, and the sacrifice is weaker. } 18. Nd1 Rxf4 19. Qxf4 Bh6 { Slightly worse. }) (17... Rxf4 { Carlsen's move! Brave, and the engine is not convinced. } 18. Qxf4 Bh6 19. Qg3 Qf8 { He keeps the balance, and you are the exchange down. Slightly worse. }) 0-1


