{ New plan: space. Cramp him with a pawn, trade his good bishop, then invade. Push the f pawn. [%cal Yf4f5][%csl Rc8] }
12. f5 { Pawn to f5! His bishop on c8 is buried, e6 is yours, and f4 is free for a bishop trade. [%csl Rc8,Ge6][%cal Gc1f4] } (12. a3 { A quiet move, and he is ready for f5 now. } 12... b6 13. f5 Bb7 { The bishop got out first. Slightly worse. [%csl Gb7] }) (12. Kf2 { The king first. } 12... b6 13. Re1 Bb7 { Slightly worse. }) (12. Bd2 { Development, and his a pawn runs. } 12... a5 13. Rae1 a4 { His pawns roll. Slightly worse. }) (12. h3 { Slow. } 12... a5 13. a3 Bd7 { Slightly worse. }) 12... b6 { He wants the bishop on b7. Trade his good bishop first. [%cal Yc1f4] } 13. Bf4 { Bishop to f4: his dark bishop is his good one, and now it goes. [%cal Gf4d6] } (13. a3 { Slow, and the bishop pair stays. } 13... Bb7 14. Bf4 Bxf4 { The same, a move later. }) (13. g4 { A pawn storm without the trade. } 13... Bb7 14. Bf4 Bxf4 { The same, a move later. }) (13. h3 { Slow. } 13... Bb7 14. Bf4 Bxf4 { The same. }) (13. a4 { A pawn on the edge. } 13... Bb7 14. Bf4 Bxf4 { The same. }) 13... Bxf4 { He takes. Take back. [%cal Yf1f4] } 14. Rxf4 { The rook takes back and sits on f4. Now the knight: to a4, hitting b6 and c5. [%csl Gf4][%cal Gc3a4] } 14... c5 { He pushes. Now the knight. [%cal Yc3a4] } 15. Na4 { Knight to a4: b6 and c5 are targets, and d6 is a hole. Constrain, then invade. [%cal Ga4b6,Ga4c5][%csl Gd6] } (15. Rd1 { The rook takes the column. Also good. } 15... Bb7 16. Rf2 Rab8 { Still better. }) (15. Nd2 { The knight goes to c4. Fine, slower. } 15... Rb8 16. Nc4 Rd8 { Still better. }) (15. Rf2 { A rook move. } 15... Rb8 16. Nd2 Bb7 { Still better. }) (15. a4 { The pawn on the edge. } 15... Rb8 16. a5 c4 { Still better. }) (15. Nd4 { The knight jumps, and the pawn takes it. } 15... cxd4 { A whole knight. [%csl Rd4] }) 1-0


