{ The c column is open and yours. A rook alone is not enough. Bring the queen behind it, and invade. }
1. Qc2 { Queen to c2: the c column is a battery, and c7 is the target. [%cal Gc2c7][%csl Gc7] } (1. h4 { A pawn move first. Also good, one move slower. } 1... b5 2. Qc2 Qb6 { Still winning. }) (1. h3 { Slow. } 1... b5 2. Qc2 Qb6 { Still winning. }) (1. Qd1 { The queen goes the wrong way. } 1... b5 2. Qc2 Qb6 { You come to c2 anyway. Still better. }) (1. Bb4 { The bishop moves, and f6 kicks it. } 1... f6 2. Qc2 a5 { Still better, but slower. }) (1. Bxe7 { A free pawn? } 1... Qxe7 { A bishop for a pawn. [%csl Re7] }) 1... a5 { He pushes. Now the knight jumps. } 2. Ne5 { Knight to e5: it blocks his bishop and hits the knight on e4. [%csl Ge5] } (2. Qc7 { Also good: straight in. } 2... Qxc7 3. Rxc7 Ba6 { The rook is on the seventh. Winning. }) (2. h3 { Slow. } 2... Bf6 3. Qc7 Ba6 { Still winning. }) (2. h4 { Slow. } 2... Bf6 3. h5 Na6 { Still winning. }) (2. g3 { Slow. } 2... Bf6 3. Qc7 Ba6 { Still winning. }) 2... Bxe5 { He trades. Take back. } 3. dxe5 { The pawn takes back and shuts his knight in. } (3. Qc7 { The queen jumps in first, and the bishop eats it. } 3... Bxc7 { A whole queen. [%csl Rc7] }) (3. Bxe4 { You take the knight, and his bishop escapes. } 3... Bd6 4. Bxd6 Qxd6 { Everything is traded. Only a little better. }) 3... Ng5 { The knight retreats. Now invade. } 4. Qc7 { Queen to c7! He must trade, and your rook lands on the seventh. [%cal Gc7d8,Gc1c7] } (4. f4 { You kick the knight first. Also good, slower. } 4... Ne6 5. f5 Nc5 { Still winning. }) (4. Bb5 { The bishop hits nothing. } 4... Ne6 5. f4 Kh8 { Still winning, slower. }) (4. Be2 { Slow. } 4... Ne6 5. Bb5 d4 { Still better. }) (4. h4 { The pawn kicks the knight. } 4... Ne6 5. Bb5 d4 { Still better. }) 1-0
